From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:47:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] hw/arm/chumby_classic: Add the keypad port and the top
 button

The Chumby's top button (the "squeeze switch", /dev/switch in the stock
kernel) is on the i.MX21 keypad port, used as GPIO: the stock driver
polls the data register and reads row 0, low while pressed. With the
keypad registers reading back what was written, the button read as
held all the time.

Add a model of the keypad port whose data register reads the pins
configured as inputs (pulled up unless driven), and a "button" property
on the machine that drives row 0: qom-set /machine button true presses
the button and false releases it. The machine becomes a QOM subclass
to carry the property.

Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
